 "story": "The labor market re-accelerated in August \u2014 payrolls +162K against a 55K consensus, June\u2013July revised up, and initial claims back under 200K \u2014 just as inflation proved sticky: headline CPI held at 3.4% with a hot 0.3% core print and PPI climbed to 5.4% on energy. That combination pushed the Fed to its first hike under Chair Warsh (+25 bp to 3.75\u20134.00% on Sep 16). Rate-sensitive housing is the casualty: builder sentiment hit a one-year low, starts and permits missed, and the 30-yr mortgage rate is back near 7% with the 10-yr near 5%. Manufacturing surveys remain in expansion (ISM 54.6) even as factory output stalled. Equities have looked through it, with the S&P 500 up 13.4% YTD.",
 "consensus_policy": "Consensus = Bloomberg survey median as reported in First Trust Data Watch; Dow Jones, LSEG, Reuters or FactSet where noted or where Bloomberg is not public. \u201c\u2014\u201d = no public consensus.",
 "actuals_policy": "Actual = value as first published on release day (ALFRED vintage), cross-checked against the agency release. Later revisions appear in Notes."
